  "descriptions": {
    "preferred": "The distinct yellowgreen foliage makes this cultivar worthwhile. The green tones of the large leaves darken as summer progresses. Fall color is yellow, occasionally tinged orange. The five to seven deeply separated lobes are incised and toothed along the margins but not as deeply cut to the midrib as in most dissectums. This plant is very vigorous and matures at 8 ft. (2. 5 m) high and 10 ft. (3 m) wide. The name means \"yellowish. \""
  },
